## Make MCP graph tools work without a sticky session
================================================================================

Context: Issue #209 — Databricks AI Playground opens a new StreamableHTTP
session per tool call, so select_domain keyed by mcp-session-id never
reaches the next graph tool. Keep per-session isolation (issue #185) and
resolve the domain from an optional domain_name argument, MCP_DEFAULT_DOMAIN,
or the only published MCP domain.

Changes:

1. src/mcp-server/server/session.py
   Add resolve_domain_name / require_domain (async) / lazy class-action cache.
2. src/mcp-server/server/tools.py
   Optional domain_name on every domain-scoped tool; share class-action ingest.
3. src/mcp-server/server/factory.py
   Instruct clients to pass domain_name when the session is not reused.
4. tests/units/mcp/test_session_isolation.py
   Cover explicit / env / unique-domain resolution without leaking sessions.
5. tests/units/mcp/test_domain_policy_gating.py
   Cover Playground-style get_status and policy with domain_name, no select.
6. tests/mcp/integration/test_more_smoke_tools.py
   Two-domain registry so the unique fallback does not hide a missing select.
7. tests/mcp/test_tool_http_boundary.py
   Assert identity on the GraphQL hop when policy preload adds extra GETs.
8. docs/mcp.md
   Document Playground one-shot sessions, MCP_DEFAULT_DOMAIN, and OPT 2 limits.
9. docs/user-guide.md
   Same Playground guidance; drop the stale process-global selected-domain note.

